### Payment Verification System

All payment applications will be reviewed manually by the Super Admin.

Payment statuses:

- Pending
- Approved
- Rejected

When a payment request is submitted:

1. Store the application in the database.
2. Mark it as Pending.
3. Notify the Super Admin.
4. Display its status to the restaurant owner.

The Super Admin will verify the transaction against the relevant payment-provider transaction record.

Only after successful verification can Lifetime Access be activated.

Do not pretend that a transaction has been automatically verified without an actual provider integration or manual verification.

### Duplicate Transaction Protection

Transaction IDs must be globally unique across all restaurant accounts.

If a user submits an already-used Transaction ID:

- Prevent the submission.
- Display a Duplicate Transaction ID warning.
- Do not create another valid payment application.

### Rejected Payment

If the Super Admin finds an invalid Transaction ID:

- Reject the payment application.
- Save the rejection reason.
- Display Rejected status in the restaurant Dashboard.
- Display the rejection reason.

The restaurant owner can submit a new application using the correct Transaction ID.

