# 8. Direct Restaurant Billing System

Create a fast and professional billing interface.

There will be no table management system.

There will be no table numbers, reserved tables or occupied-table management.

The billing flow will be direct dine-in billing.

Do not create separate takeaway or home-delivery order workflows.

### Food Selection Interface

Display food categories.

When a user selects a category, show the corresponding food items as large, attractive buttons.

Food buttons must display:

- Food Name
- Food Price

### Food Selection Behaviour

When the user clicks a food button:

- Add one unit of that food to the bill.

When the same food button is clicked again:

- Increase its quantity by one.
- Do not create a separate duplicate line.

### Quantity Controls

Provide:

- Plus (+) button.
- Minus (-) button.
- Direct numerical quantity input.

Quantity must never become zero or negative while an item remains in the bill.

### Bill Calculation

For every item:

Item Total = Unit Price × Quantity

Grand Total = Sum of all item totals.

The calculation must update automatically whenever the quantity changes.

